{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad","id":1536701,"title":"Why did the wyrm go bad?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-02T09:50:20-07:00","id":1536701,"title":"Why did the wyrm go bad?","content":"what could have possibly caused the very concept of entropy itself to be irreversibly corrupted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T11:14:45-07:00","id":1536703,"title":"","content":"It was trapped in the Weavers webs and fractured itself trying to escape...those fractured parts of its personality are each trying different means to escape and turning in upon themselves as they do so.<br /> <br /> The Weaver did this as she did not appreciate the Wyrms destruction of her creations as part of the cycle and sought to stop it from doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T11:15:25-07:00","id":1536704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad#post1536701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what could have possibly caused the very concept of entropy itself to be irreversibly corrupted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um.It's literally said in the books. Once upon a time the Weaver was tired of everything it ever made changing and everything dying. So it tried to contain the Wyld, but it was too fluid to contain. Then it wrapped the Wyrm in its webs seeking to control it and direct it. Alas, it was an unstoppable force hitting an immoveable object and in the process casused the Wyrm to become insane ans obsessed with everything suffering and dying as it did.<br /> <br /> It's not that it's irreversibly corrupted, it's more along the lines that it still does what it was meant to (that's why we still have death, decay and the circle of life), but parts of it are hell bent on murdering everything and torturing it until breaks and all falls down into utter nothingness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T11:37:02-07:00","id":1536706,"title":"","content":"For me, the entire fun of the whole Spirit Triat thing, is that they should work in unison, munching their part of reality forward to the next, in a big triangular circle of life-matter-time.<br /> <br /> But then, it got unbalanced somehow, most stories tell of the Weaver imprisoning it, for it superseded its own function, wanting to turn everything created Stactic. So it left Wyld alone, so it could create new stuff for it to edify, and locked Wyrm to stop it from destroying that which weaved. <br /> One detail for me, is that Wyld will inevitably either have less material to work with, cuz Wyrm dismantled the materials of creation so that Wyld could spit them out renewed and bent on new things. Or it will be the opposite, having so much creating to do that it becomes unhinged.<br /> <br /> Either way, unbalancing the Triat is like screwing with one third or more of a a big machine composed of three sides, with each size not being 'one thing' but a junction of hundreds of small gears, in a way that they either work very badly or go overdrive. I like to think different werewolf Tribes, and different supernatural groups, will either believe the world needs one side to take over the others, or that one faltering side be brought back to shape just so all can be in unison once again. <br /> If the Wyrm is nuts, than you gotta regulate that which is causing it, which is the Weaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T14:30:20-07:00","id":1536717,"title":"","content":"Different answer:<br /> <br /> Humans.<br /> <br /> While the books tend to lay the blame on the Weaver, they also tend to do so from the unreliable narrator perspective when touching on such matters. Though this is also something that evolved as the game did. In early WtA the Weaver wasn't treated nearly as seriously as a threat, but that changed as the 90s chugged along a the idea that the Weaver wasn't ascendant didn't really reflect &quot;our world but darker&quot; well. Hence the books started to treat &quot;the Weaver is to blame&quot;as more of the default because at a minimum it would be very hard for the characters in the setting to see it as anything other than this.<br /> <br /> But that somewhat ignores what caused the Weaver to suddenly lose sight of its place in the Triat. The Weaver might have struck the first blow in the Triat falling out of balance, but that just shifts the question the OP asked: what could have possibly caused the Weaver to become corrupted from its purpose? &quot;The Weaver just went overboard with its duties, after untold eons of doing it right,&quot; isn't really much of an answer there.<br /> <br /> The books also offer plenty on my differing answer. The rise of humanity is pretty much directly linked to everything going wrong in the WtA cosmology. Humans being out of touch with spirituality and true natural wilderness has always been a core of the game. Humans, even normal ignorant ones, have an immensely outsized influence on the animistic spirits of the setting. Every other animal naturally exists within the (not very pleasant) natural order equated with Gaia herself; existing in a state of homeostatic balance that the Triat stems from instead of the other way around. Humans are (possibly inherently) the one that embody the Triat first, and honor Gaia second, instead of the other way around. Humans created imbalance in the Triat by giving the Triat something to actually want to fight over. There was finally something in the Tellurian that could give one member of the Triat power over the others. The whole concept of the &quot;anthropocene epoch&quot; very neatly aligns with, well, everything going wrong; including the Fera going at each other and the Wars of Rage starting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T07:00:08-07:00","id":1537203,"title":"","content":"It also depends on the Triat's relationship to Gaia. Sometimes Gaia is presented as the creator of the Triat, sometimes the Triat is presented as a universal element while Gaia is local to the Earth and associated Umbra. In the latter case, there probably isn't an understandable explanation for how the Weaver and Wyrm corrupted unless it is only a local corruption. That said, the idea that Werewolves have even the slightest hope of fighting the Wyrm or restoring its balance implies that the problem is more local (if you can call the entire Earth and associated Umbra local).<br /> <br /> If Gaia created them, it is important to remember that she is not depicted as perfect and she certainly does not create perfect, unchanging beings. Her creations are flawed and adaptive. If she creates a balance it is not one of a perfectly balanced scale, but of a tightrope walker who is moment by moment adjusting to maintain that balance; a constant series of destabilizations and momentary equilibriums. . Nothing pushes towards balance, everything (including her &quot;guardians&quot;) actually pushes towards imbalance, just in different directions. Usually this ends up pushing the world back towards some new balance, though there is no certainty it always will. <br /> <br /> If the Triat are her creations they would be the same: their metaphysical balance would be created not by some ideal harmony but by constant competition. If that is the case, nothing happened to the Weaver to make her fight the Wyrm, she was always doing that anyways. What was different was her assault was particularly effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T10:34:26-07:00","id":1537209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537203#post1537203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also depends on the Triat's relationship to Gaia. Sometimes Gaia is presented as the creator of the Triat, sometimes the Triat is presented as a universal element while Gaia is local to the Earth and associated Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never within W:tA, usually from the perspective of other games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the latter case, there probably isn't an understandable explanation for how the Weaver and Wyrm corrupted unless it is only a local corruption. That said, the idea that Werewolves have even the slightest hope of fighting the Wyrm or restoring its balance implies that the problem is more local (if you can call the entire Earth and associated Umbra local). </div> </div> </div>Not even remotely! You just have to make allowances for them going closer to the way of Exalted, and potentially having to sacrifice themselves to make it work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Gaia created them, it is important to remember that she is not depicted as perfect and she certainly does not create perfect, unchanging beings. Her creations are flawed and adaptive. If she creates a balance it is not one of a perfectly balanced scale, but of a tightrope walker who is moment by moment adjusting to maintain that balance; a constant series of destabilizations and momentary equilibriums. . Nothing pushes towards balance, everything (including her &quot;guardians&quot;) actually pushes towards imbalance, just in different directions. Usually this ends up pushing the world back towards some new balance, though there is no certainty it always will. </div> </div> </div>It's a bit more stable than that, typically. When two whole thirds are trying to make trouble, then it's a tightrope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Triat are her creations they would be the same: their metaphysical balance would be created not by some ideal harmony but by constant competition. If that is the case, nothing happened to the Weaver to make her fight the Wyrm, she was always doing that anyways. What was different was her assault was particularly effective. </div> </div> </div>Fighting them is one thing, kidnapping them and then burying them in a coffin is something else entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T16:57:26-07:00","id":1537238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537209#post1537209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never within W:tA, usually from the perspective of other games.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But that's because WtA has no perspective on the universe as a whole, it focus exclusively on Earth.<br /> <br /> In fact only Mage spends any time whatsoever considering that our planet may not be the center of the universe. But it is less that WtA assumes Gaia and the Triat are universal forces and more that it doesn't even stop to consider the question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T21:03:06-07:00","id":1537246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537238#post1537238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's because WtA has no perspective on the universe as a whole, it focus exclusively on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're given information about the Aetherial Realm out of character, with no unreliable narrator. Distant, cosmic objects that can be reached much more quickly in the Aetherial Realm have a Triatic bent, and bleed into the Deep Umbra, so I'd say that this notion is not even remotely true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact only Mage spends any time whatsoever considering that our planet may not be the center of the universe. But it is less that WtA assumes Gaia and the Triat are universal forces and more that it doesn't even stop to consider the question. </div> </div> </div>Mage, however, assumes that humans are the most important thing. However many steps forward, an infinity backward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T00:59:45-07:00","id":1537254,"title":"","content":"Besides the fact that WtA and MtA both have (small, fringe, and generally ignored) factions that are actively trying to use the Umbra to reach other solar systems in the hopes of finding out if they have their own &quot;center&quot; just like the Umbra around Earth does (and thus could be a safe haven since the one around Earth in the WoD is screwed), it's ultimately not something any of the games really get into because it's so far removed from the central dramatic conflict of the game. The games leave it at, &quot;there's no Umbral explorer with the power or skill to make it to another place far enough away to answer,&quot; because it allows for in-game speculation without removing the immediacy of the threats going on now in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T07:48:29-07:00","id":1537259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537209#post1537209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a bit more stable than that, typically. When two whole thirds are trying to make trouble, then it's a tightrope.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tightrope walker was the description of all of it, because a tightrope walker is constantly adjusting and rebalancing to fit the next situation he is in. The truly great imbalances can make him fall, yes, but he's always reacting. It's the balance of a forest, never the same from year to year.<br /> <br /> Where the tightrope walker analogy breaks down is that the performer intentionally balances himself while Gaia's balance is more about unintentional balancing. Deer don't try to manage their own populations, nor do wolves try to manage deer populations or their own. Instead they unintentional push each other towards equilibrium, and that equilibrium changes from year to year.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T14:52:41-07:00","id":1537277,"title":"","content":"The biome equilibrium analogy really doesn't work on a number of levels (also, biome stability is not something you can measure year-to-year, that's like conflating weather and climate).<br /> <br /> The biggest issue is that wolves and deer don't intentionally work towards a balance for a number of reasons, including that balance being beyond their ability to comprehend. Gaia created beings with the ability to perceive and comprehend the state of balance in the system, and then actively get involved. The WtA is not built on a system of mindless actors. Gaia, the Triat, the Celestines, the Incarnae and all their brood, the shifters... they're all conscious intelligent actors on the system. Regardless of how one wants to position Gaia vs. the Triat in hierarchy, Gaia wanted intentional actors in the system. The WoD is an animist world where the wolves and the deer are being steered by forces they don't recognize, but are not just the natural processes of real world evolution either.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Weaver just landed a particularly effective attack,&quot; again, doesn't really explain anything. It just takes it as an axiomatic truth that this was always possible and thus over along enough period of time one of the Triat would destabilize the system irrevocably. But the only evidence of that is that it happened, creating a circular argument at best. We know stable-tension systems exist. Tension systems are not inherently subject to probabilistic ends where every moment is an extremely low probability event that the system breaks and it's just when we finally get that one in a vastly huge number chance event. Most tension systems will fail eventually, but also predictably rather than on probability (even if we, as imperfect beings, need to rely on statistics to estimate when that will be). IRL, we know that baring an external event disrupting things, the Earth's orbit around the sun is stable enough that it will last until the sun starts to increase in size and then swallows the Earth. That is the knowable end result of the gravity-tensions of the solar system we live in. It's not a matter of &quot;when will one gravity-body disrupt the system first.&quot; We can't measure things precisely enough to give an exact date to when this will happen, but we can make a very good prediction considering the time scales involved.<br /> <br /> It is, of course, possible for something to change that equilibrium that's not in the current equation. Any number of celestial events could knock Earth out of orbit, or just generally mess everything up. And we can't really predict any of them reasonably (we know our galaxy is on a collision course with another galaxy, but galaxies are so big and mostly empty, we have no idea how disruptive that will be &quot;locally&quot;). <br /> <br /> Since I see no compelling reason to assume the tension based stabilize of the Triat is inherently probabilistic in its internal equilibrium, the best answer to why things change is always going to be the introduction of something new to the system. And the books provide a direct answer to that: humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T14:58:54-07:00","id":1537278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537246#post1537246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're given information about the Aetherial Realm out of character, with no unreliable narrator. Distant, cosmic objects that can be reached much more quickly in the Aetherial Realm have a Triatic bent, and bleed into the Deep Umbra, so I'd say that this notion is not even remotely true.</div> </div> </div> </div>The \u00c6therial is itself an umbral realm that exists from the perspective of Earth, and only reaches part of our solar system.<br /> <br /> It says nothing about what would we find and experience from the perspective of an actual native resident of another planet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537246#post1537246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mage, however, assumes that humans are the most important thing. However many steps forward, an infinity backward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, what's the point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-12T18:17:43-07:00","id":1537282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537278#post1537278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The \u00c6therial is itself an umbral realm that exists from the perspective of Earth, and only reaches part of our solar system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last time I checked, there weren't any black holes in our solar system, but there are some that are close to the Aetherial. Plenty of other objects drift through it to paint a picture that it extends far beyond the bounds of Earth's solar system.<br /> <br /> What's more, the game takes the stance that even if you did find extrasolar life... they wouldn't be in any position to help. Quite possibly, you're looking at a Dead Space situation. That's what Revised went with, in the end, to help emphasize the kind of showdown that the Apocalypse is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It says nothing about what would we find and experience from the perspective of an actual native resident of another planet.<br /> <br /> Indeed, what's the point? </div> </div> </div>If you think that the Garou perspective is limited, allow me to introduce you to a crop of folk who thinks that outer space <b>is</b> the spirit world...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T09:29:15-07:00","id":1537308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537277#post1537277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biome equilibrium analogy really doesn't work on a number of levels (also, biome stability is not something you can measure year-to-year, that's like conflating weather and climate).<br /> <br /> The biggest issue is that wolves and deer don't intentionally work towards a balance for a number of reasons, including that balance being beyond their ability to comprehend. Gaia created beings with the ability to perceive and comprehend the state of balance in the system, and then actively get involved. The WtA is not built on a system of mindless actors. Gaia, the Triat, the Celestines, the Incarnae and all their brood, the shifters... they're all conscious intelligent actors on the system. Regardless of how one wants to position Gaia vs. the Triat in hierarchy, Gaia wanted intentional actors in the system. The WoD is an animist world where the wolves and the deer are being steered by forces they don't recognize, but are not just the natural processes of real world evolution either.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are always levels analogies don't work on. There's nothing surprising there. If they get the idea across they've done their job. Seems like this one did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Weaver just landed a particularly effective attack,&quot; again, doesn't really explain anything. </div> </div> </div>That wasn't the point, though. The point was to address how the Weaver decided to attack the Wyrm in the first place, not to figure out why a particular move was super effective. However, you yourself do a great job of tackling why this time it was:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since I see no compelling reason to assume the tension based stabilize of the Triat is inherently probabilistic in its internal equilibrium, the best answer to why things change is always going to be the introduction of something new to the system. And the books provide a direct answer to that: humans. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The only thing I'd add is that humans are just one of countless things added over the eons. Certainly it is thematically appropriate to the game that humans are a key part of the current problem, but their entry into the world is not unique. Indeed I don't think there is a specific answer on whether the extinction of the dinosaurs happened before or after the corruption of the Wyrm. Humans may not have even existed when the Weaver made her big move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T09:59:55-07:00","id":1537311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537308#post1537308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like this one did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very confused then, because you said Gaia's balance was on of unintentional actors, and I pointed out that intentional actors are clearly part of her intent in the books. The &quot;wolves and deer&quot; who balance each other via instinct instead of the tightrope walker that balances out of intention was the point you were making... but you're saying that your analogy made it's point while agreeing that it's something that isn't fulling intentional or fully unintentional... so yeah, confusion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point was to address how the Weaver decided to attack the Wyrm in the first place, not to figure out why a particular move was super effective. </div> </div> </div>The possibility of a super effective attack presumes things not in evidence, something you seem to agree with?<br /> <br /> Also, the point doesn't really work. If you presume that Triat were always bickering, to go back to the wolves and deer: sometimes deer gore a wolf. That's already part of the stable tensions in the system. An explanation of &quot;why&quot; the Weaver might push against the Wyrm isn't necessary because nobody is contesting the idea that the Triat existed in a state of tension with each other. What's unexplained by focusing on the Triat is what broken the &quot;stalemate.&quot; Your point only works if you presume the stalemate was inherently unsustainable on its own, but then you agree that the most likely source of instability was an external factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Certainly it is thematically appropriate to the game that humans are a key part of the current problem, but their entry into the world is not unique. </div> </div> </div>While the entry of new things to the system isn't unique (that's the Wyld's whole job after all) humans are certainly unique given their clearly stated impact on the state of the WoD and WtA specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T10:57:31-07:00","id":1537312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537311#post1537311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm very confused then, because you said Gaia's balance was on of unintentional actors, and I pointed out that intentional actors are clearly part of her intent in the books. The &quot;wolves and deer&quot; who balance each other via instinct instead of the tightrope walker that balances out of intention was the point you were making... but you're saying that your analogy made it's point while agreeing that it's something that isn't fulling intentional or fully unintentional... so yeah, confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see the issue. I said that the actors don't have to be intentionally balancing themselves, not that they had no intentions at all. I hope that clears things up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The possibility of a super effective attack presumes things not in evidence, something you seem to agree with? </div> </div> </div>It's not something I went that deeply into before your previous post. I'm not going to preclude the possibility of the Weaver just getting a super effective attack in on her own, if that's what you are asking, but I think it far more satisfying on both a metaphysical and dramatic level if their struggle is intertwined with the rest of creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the point doesn't really work. If you presume that Triat were always bickering, to go back to the wolves and deer: sometimes deer gore a wolf. That's already part of the stable tensions in the system. An explanation of &quot;why&quot; the Weaver might push against the Wyrm isn't necessary because nobody is contesting the idea that the Triat existed in a state of tension with each other. What's unexplained by focusing on the Triat is what broken the &quot;stalemate.&quot; Your point only works if you presume the stalemate was inherently unsustainable on its own, but then you agree that the most likely source of instability was an external factor. </div> </div> </div>I'm having a hard time figuring out which of my points you are referring to. What you are responding to is my point that the Weaver did not need to be corrupt or imbalanced to try and attack or trap the Wyrm. That point works regardless of whether the system is sustainable or not.<br /> <br /> I do agree that significant changes to the system, like the introduction of humans, make major imbalances more both more likely and more narratively coherent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While the entry of new things to the system isn't unique (that's the Wyld's whole job after all) humans are certainly unique given their clearly stated impact on the state of the WoD and WtA specifically. </div> </div> </div>At the very least they are notably different than most other creations. Whether they are unique in that regard is unclear. Again, as I recall one of the given possibilities is that the Wyrm fell before humans ever existed. If we run with the idea that humans are an imbalancing force on the system, then it implies that there are other entities with comparable effects.<br /> <br /> That, or human influence predated human existence. That's very possible but not usually the way the WoD approaches events.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T19:56:53-07:00","id":1537327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537282#post1537282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Last time I checked, there weren't any black holes in our solar system, but there are some that are close to the Aetherial. Plenty of other objects drift through it to paint a picture that it extends far beyond the bounds of Earth's solar system.<br /> <br /> What's more, the game takes the stance that even if you did find extrasolar life... they wouldn't be in any position to help. Quite possibly, you're looking at a Dead Space situation. That's what Revised went with, in the end, to help emphasize the kind of showdown that the Apocalypse is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying anything about help from aliens or whatever. I'm saying the \u00c6therial isn't the &quot;real&quot; Outer Space, it is an umbral realm that exists from Earth's POV.<br /> <br /> This POV may or may not be objectively true, it may or may not be the only one that exists, it is surely the only one we are presented with. But it is still the Earth's POV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537282#post1537282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you think that the Garou perspective is limited, allow me to introduce you to a crop of folk who thinks that outer space <b>is</b> the spirit world...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no, but so what?<br /> <br /> My point from the beginning is just that WtA don't talk about cosmic scales because that's not the point for the game. it isn't the point of any WoD game.<br /> <br /> Stop seeing everything as an attack on Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T22:53:46-07:00","id":1537332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537327#post1537327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not saying anything about help from aliens or whatever. I'm saying the \u00c6therial isn't the &quot;real&quot; Outer Space, it is an umbral realm that exists from Earth's POV.<br /> <br /> This POV may or may not be objectively true, it may or may not be the only one that exists, it is surely the only one we are presented with. But it is still the Earth's POV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that you can potentially commit suicide by stepping sideways on another planet's Aetherial representation - which then places you on the actual planet in the physical Realm, far, far away from Earth, and in a pickle that only Adaptation could save you from. The Aetherial Realm has very much been presented as the Umbra, but in Space, for a very long time in the line, and not just a belief or representation that isn't really it. It's not an outer space Arcadia Gateway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes and no, but so what?<br /> <br /> My point from the beginning is just that WtA don't talk about cosmic scales because that's not the point for the game. it isn't the point of any WoD game. </div> </div> </div>Technically it talks about cosmic scales as scary shit that have to be stopped from being enacted because &quot;there is no garden in which to flee&quot;. W:tA otherwise talks a lot about the cosmic significance of success for the gribblies on Earth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Stop seeing everything as an attack on Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>Bringing Mage into a conversation about Werewolf is basically stating that you're going to assume that W:tA is completely wrong, which is an odd tack to take in a thread about setting elements from W:tA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T18:28:51-07:00","id":1537377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537332#post1537332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that you can potentially commit suicide by stepping sideways on another planet's Aetherial representation - which then places you on the actual planet in the physical Realm, far, far away from Earth, and in a pickle that only Adaptation could save you from. The Aetherial Realm has very much been presented as the Umbra, but in Space, for a very long time in the line, and not just a belief or representation that isn't really it. It's not an outer space Arcadia Gateway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being connected doesn't preclude being an Earth-centered Realm. It is, after all, an umbral realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537332#post1537332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bringing Mage into a conversation about Werewolf is basically stating that you're going to assume that W:tA is completely wrong, which is an odd tack to take in a thread about setting elements from W:tA.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just mentioned it in passing, and by no means I meant that, nor do I think such a preposterous notion could be inferred from what I said.<br /> <br /> What I said is that WtA doesn't explore the rest of the universe. And it doesn't. The game is focused on Earth. All and every assertion made within it, can only be made from the perspective of Earth dwellers.<br /> <br /> Forget the fucking Mage comment, I am assuming the WtA cosmology and none other when I say this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T22:49:14-07:00","id":1537380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537377#post1537377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being connected doesn't preclude being an Earth-centered Realm. It is, after all, an umbral realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an odd one out. While identified as an Umbra Realm, it's more of an extension of the Middle Penumbra over the entire universe. Kind of like how while Malfeas is also identified as an Umbral Realm, it's something far, far different from the rest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just mentioned it in passing, and by no means I meant that, nor do I think such a preposterous notion could be inferred from what I said.<br /> <br /> What I said is that WtA doesn't explore the rest of the universe. And it doesn't. The game is focused on Earth. All and every assertion made within it, can only be made from the perspective of Earth dwellers.<br /> <br /> Forget the fucking Mage comment, I am assuming the WtA cosmology and none other when I say this. </div> </div> </div>The adventure in Rage Across the Heavens explores the universe while also being centered on what happens on Earth. The Perfect Crinos-born can really bend setting assumptions left and right. The Aetherial Realm also allows for much easier space travel than even what the Technocracy's anachronistic ships enjoy, and Adaptation explicitly notes that it allows a character to live on other planets or out in space, so it doesn't seem so nearly cut and dried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T17:02:17-07:00","id":1537442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1536701-why-did-the-wyrm-go-bad?p=1537380#post1537380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an odd one out. While identified as an Umbra Realm, it's more of an extension of the Middle Penumbra over the entire universe. Kind of like how while Malfeas is also identified as an Umbral Realm, it's something far, far different from the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, indeed, and I'm not saying that things are cut and dry, quite the opposite: as the setting describes all that from a particular POV (or several, but all earth-bound), there is some space in it to say the Triat is bigger in scope than Gaia. And sometimes this is hinted to be a possibility.<br /> <br /> But if this is the case or not isn't just something the setting doesn't explain, it's something it doesn't even care about, precisely because the reality of other worlds is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is about the Earth, fighting for it or against it, it is about the consequences the very world suffers and what can be done about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}